# Without this file, `COPY . .` hands Docker the whole working tree —
# including node_modules and .pnpm-store. Measured on the first build
# attempt: 6 GB of free disk consumed, and `prisma generate` failing inside
# the image because the host's darwin-arm64 query engine had been copied
# over the linux one the deps stage had just installed. Both Dockerfiles
# install dependencies themselves from the lockfile; nothing built on this
# machine belongs in an image.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output. The image builds its own; copying a host build in would ship
# whatever was last compiled here, including a dev-mode .next.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Secrets. A .env copied into an image is a secret published to everyone who
# can pull it, and it would also silently override the environment the
# container is actually given.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .certs is NOT excluded here because it holds a CA certificate, which is
# public by nature — but it is never COPYed either: the Dockerfiles take it
# as a build secret so it stays out of the finished image.

# Python virtualenv for services/rembg (~730 MB of macOS binaries) — that
# service builds from its own context and installs its own dependencies.
services/rembg/.venv

.git
.github
.superpowers
docs
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
